Subject: notifier: post "Restart is required" once, from discoverabstractnotifier.notifyrc as UpdateRestart

DiscoverNotifier::showRebootNotification() builds the notification
with the static KNotification::event(), which queues a sendEvent() of
its own, and then calls sendEvent() itself, so every restart is sent
to org.freedesktop.Notifications twice. Construct the KNotification
and set its title, text and icon instead, so the one sendEvent() posts
it once.

It also posts "UpdateRestart" with KNotification::DefaultEvent, which
makes KNotification look the event up in the default component,
plasma_workspace, instead of the discoverabstractnotifier component it
names; plasma_workspace.notifyrc declares no UpdateRestart, so
"Restart is required" is never shown. Name discoverabstractnotifier as
the component without DefaultEvent, and spell that notifyrc's group
[Event/UpdateRestart], the name the notifier posts, where it declares
[Event/UpdateResart].

--- a/libdiscover/resources/discoverabstractnotifier.notifyrc
+++ b/libdiscover/resources/discoverabstractnotifier.notifyrc
@@ -653,7 +653,7 @@
 Urgency=High
 Action=Popup
 
-[Event/UpdateResart]
+[Event/UpdateRestart]
 Name=Restart is Required
 Name[ar]=إعادة التّشغيل مطلوبة
 Name[az]=Yenidən başlatmaq tələb olunur
--- a/notifier/DiscoverNotifier.cpp
+++ b/notifier/DiscoverNotifier.cpp
@@ -414,12 +414,15 @@
         m_rebootNotification->close();
     }
 
-    KNotification *notification = KNotification::event(QStringLiteral("UpdateRestart"),
-                                                       i18n("Restart is required"),
-                                                       i18n("The system needs to be restarted for the updates to take effect."),
-                                                       QStringLiteral("system-software-update"),
-                                                       KNotification::Persistent | KNotification::DefaultEvent,
-                                                       QStringLiteral("discoverabstractnotifier"));
+    // Constructed, not KNotification::event(): that queues a sendEvent() of
+    // its own, and with the one below every restart would be posted twice.
+    // The component is named without DefaultEvent, which would look the
+    // event up in plasma_workspace, whose notifyrc does not declare it.
+    KNotification *notification = new KNotification(QStringLiteral("UpdateRestart"), KNotification::Persistent);
+    notification->setComponentName(QStringLiteral("discoverabstractnotifier"));
+    notification->setTitle(i18n("Restart is required"));
+    notification->setText(i18n("The system needs to be restarted for the updates to take effect."));
+    notification->setIconName(QStringLiteral("system-software-update"));
 
     auto restartAction = notification->addAction(i18nc("@action:button", "Update and Restart"));
     auto shutdownAction = notification->addAction(i18nc("@action:button", "Update and Shut Down"));
